invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20.c's use_avx2 answers 1 before ch_cfg.cpu exists to carry
  the caller's CH_CPU_AVX2 bit, so every x86-64 CHACHA=vector object runs
  the AVX2 kernel and dies of SIGILL on a CPU without AVX2. Every vector and
  equivalence case passes on a CPU with it, because the kernel computes
  the same bytes. The script compiles chacha20.c for x86-64 and requires
  its object to call chacha20_vector_xor and not the kernel.

--- old
static int use_avx2(void) {
    return 0;
}
--- new
static int use_avx2(void) {
    return 1;
}
